{"availability":"available","full":"hermes98761234/zero-knowledge-demos","name":"zero-knowledge-demos","description":"Interactive zero-knowledge proof playground: Schnorr, Fiat-Shamir, over-18 range proof, graph 3-colouring, Ali Baba cave, Waldo","category":"Education","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-09T19:34:08Z","updated":"2026-10-09T19:34:15Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://hermes98761234.github.io/zero-knowledge-demos/","topics":["cryptography","education","react","schnorr","zero-knowledge"],"demo":"https://hermes98761234.github.io/zero-knowledge-demos/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T19:35:09.435Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T19:35:09.435Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T19:35:09.435Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T19:35:09.435Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An interactive playground for zero-knowledge proofs: prove you know a password, that you are over 18, that a graph can be 3-coloured, or where Waldo is, without revealing the secret. Every demo shows what goes over the wire and what the verifier learns. The cryptography is real (secp256k1 through @noble/curves, hashes through @noble/hashes) and runs entirely in your browser.","Try it: hermes98761234.github.io/zero-knowledge-demos"],"features":["I know the password. Step through Schnorr identification (commit, challenge, response), run 20 rounds against a cheating prover who only passes by guessing the challenge, and watch the odds collapse. Then make it…","I am over 18. An issuer signs a Pedersen commitment to your age. You prove age - 18 lies in [0, 2^7) with a bit-decomposition range proof, each bit shown to be 0 or 1 by an OR-proof. Issuer, holder and verifier roles…","Graph 3-colouring. The Goldreich-Micali-Wigderson protocol as a game: hidden colours, the verifier picks an edge, two vertices are revealed, repeat. A non-3-colourable graph (K4) shows so